'''Ithorians''', commonly referred to as '''hammerheads''' or as '''leathernecks''' as an insult, were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] from the [[planet]] [[Ithor]]. Ithorians had two mouths on the opposite sides of their necks, giving them a deep, rumbling voice. Most Ithorians were peaceful and revered nature. The species' pacifism was so strong that they exiled violent individuals from their homeworld of Ithor. Notable Ithorians include [[Dok-Ondar]], a [[collector]] on [[Batuu]], and [[Momaw Nadon]], an Ithorian gardener who was [[Exile (punishment)|exiled]] from his homeworld.

==Biology and appearance==
[[File:OncaBulduga-Db.png|thumb|300px|left|Onca (left) and Bulduga (right), Ithorian bounty hunters and brothers]]
Ithorians, commonly referred to as "hammerheads," were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] from the [[planet]] [[Ithor]].<ref name="HtH" /> Living in the [[forest]]s or [[jungle]]s,<ref name="VE" /> Ithorians had a unique set of twin [[mouth]]s on opposite sides of their necks<ref name="Ithorians" /> with four throats, making them speak in stereo<ref name="Alien Archive" /> with deep, rumbling voices.<ref name="Ithorians" /> They had two stomachs.<ref name="In the Name of Honor">{{BOBF|Chapter 7: In the Name of Honor}}</ref> Their unique throat structure prevented them from speaking [[Galactic Basic Standard]], although this was mitigated by a number of devices, such as the [[translator collar]], which allowed translation from [[Ithorese]] into Basic.<ref name="USWNE">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> They could be [[Force-sensitive]].<ref name="Byph" />

Ithorians were called "leathernecks" as an insult by [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[stormtrooper]]s.<ref name="RebelBluff">{{InsiderCite|158|Rebel Bluff}}</ref> The [[Ottegan]] species were a genetic offshoot of the Ithorians, and had a similar physiology, possessing only one mouth instead of two.<ref name="Aliens of the Galaxy" />

==Society and culture==
Most Ithorians were peaceful and revered nature. The species' pacifism was so strong that they exiled violent individuals from their homeworld of Ithor. They considered Ithor sacred and strictly prohibited [[hunting]] on the planet's surface.<ref name="Bait">{{InsiderCite|162|Bait}}</ref> Though Ithorians tended to their forest gardens on Ithor,<ref name="VE" /> a majority of the planet's surface was covered with the [[Mother Jungle]], a vast rainforest that the Ithorians considered sacred, forbidding anyone from setting foot within.<ref name="Scum and Villainy">''[[Star Wars: Scum and Villainy: Case Files on the Galaxy's Most Notorious]]''</ref>

The Ithorians were organized into [[Ithorian herd|herds]], extended tribes connected by tradition and intermarriage.<ref name="Unlimited Power">''[[Unlimited Power]]''</ref>

Ithorian culture valued nature, handcrafting several spiritual objects. [[Ithorian totem]]s were hand-carved from stone and marked an Ithorian's grave, giving it a deep spiritual meaning on Ithor. [[Ithorian wind chime|Ithorian Weather Chimes]] were handcrafted and prayed to for fertile soil and good weather for gardening.<ref name="Traveler's Guide">''[[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge: Traveler's Guide to Batuu]]''</ref>

==History==
The Ithorians, who worshiped Mother Jungle, long ago vowed to keep their [[homeworld]] of Ithor pristine. They moved their herds into great [[Ithorian herd ship|floating cities]] in the skies of Ithor, and eventually out into space.<ref name="Unlimited Power" />

==Ithorians in the galaxy==
[[File:Ithorian-SWTVE.jpg|thumb|right|300px|An Ithorian]]
Ithorians could be found spread across [[the galaxy]] on planets such as [[Coruscant]]<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref> and in at least one [[City|settlement]] on the planet [[Takobo]], known as [[Hammertown]].<ref name="The Future of the Force" /> They could even be found in places almost completely devoid of vegetation such as [[Momaw Nadon's garden|Momaw Nadon's hidden garden]] on [[Tatooine]].<ref name="SWCT">{{SWCT|set=Base Series 1|cardname=Momaw Nadon - Cantina Patron}}</ref> Though Ithorians were best known as peaceful horticulturists, many Ithorians put their gardening past behind them as they spread throughout the galaxy.<ref name="Traveler's Guide" />

Multiple Ithorians could be found on the planet Tatooine.<ref name="Alien Archive" /><ref name="The Tribes of Tatooine">{{BOBF|Chapter 2: The Tribes of Tatooine}}</ref> Momaw Nadon was an Ithorian [[Gender|male]] who was exiled off his homeworld for revealing the agricultural secrets of his species to the [[Galactic Empire]] in order to protect the planet. He would later live on the planet Tatooine and could often be seen in [[Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina]] in the [[city]] [[Mos Eisley]].<ref name="Alien Archive" /> [[Mok Shaiz]] was an Ithorian male who served as [[mayor]] of the city [[Mos Espa]] on Tatooine during [[Boba Fett]]'s takeover of [[Boba Fett's Palace|Jabba's palace]] during the [[New Republic Era]].<ref name="The Tribes of Tatooine" />

Dok-Ondar was a famous Ithorian collector who resided in [[Dok-Ondar's Den of Antiquities]] on the planet Batuu. At over 240 [[Standard year|years]] old, Ondar was the most infamous resident of [[Black Spire Outpost]], hosting a collection of rare and unique items.<ref name="Traveler's Guide Age" /> Multiple Ithorians were members of the [[Jedi Order]] including the [[Jedi Initiate]] [[Byph]],<ref name="Byph" /> [[Jedi Knight]] [[Mikkel Sutmani]],<ref name="Light of the Jedi">''[[The High Republic: Light of the Jedi]]''</ref> and [[Jedi]] [[Roron Corobb]].<ref name="Lightsabers">''[[Star Wars Lightsabers: A Guide to Weapons of the Force]]''</ref>

Though Ithorians were stereotyped as peaceful gardeners and [[philosopher]]s, not all Ithorians matched those descriptions. [[Bulduga]] and [[Onca]] were cunning Ithorian [[bounty hunter]]s<ref name="Bulduga">{{Databank|bulduga|Bulduga}}</ref><ref name="Onca">{{Databank|onca|Onca}}</ref> while [[Baron]] [[Boolan]],<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|baron-boolan|Baron Boolan}}</ref> who in his youth was a [[Littles|Little]] within the [[Path of the Open Hand]] [[Religion|cult]],<ref name="Path of Vengeance">''[[The High Republic: Path of Vengeance]]''</ref> was an amoral scientist who became infamous<ref name="Databank" /> and joined the [[Nihil]] at the invitation of [[Eye of the Nihil|Eye]] [[Marchion Ro]] himself,<ref name="SoS 4">[[The High Republic – Shadows of Starlight 4|''The High Republic – Shadows of Starlight'' 4]]</ref> a descendant of Boolan's<ref name="EoD">''[[The High Republic: The Eye of Darkness]]''</ref> Path caretaker<ref name="Path of Vengeance" /> [[Marda Ro]].<ref name="EoD" />

